| editorial =
'''The system that works and the system that doesn't'''

The Nagoya Basho concluded today. Kotoyamada won. Asanoyama was promoted. The rankings updated. The system works.

The Akamatsu pension fund audit begins tomorrow. 12,000 workers will line up at a temporary office in Isshinji to learn whether their retirement savings exist. The system failed them.

Two systems. One produces champions. One produces victims. The difference is not complexity. It is accountability. The basho has rules, referees, and rankings. The pension fund had a SESC audit that missed ¥18B. The basho has a yokozuna promotion council. The pension fund had a board that did not question.

The IAA Commission is the new referee. The audit is the new ranking. The workers are the athletes — except they did not choose to compete. They chose to work. They chose to trust. The system broke the trust.

